1
00:00:00,366 --> 00:00:01,566
Have you ever noticed

2
00:00:01,833 --> 00:00:03,900
that the orders you really regret

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,500
were never placed during the day

4
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:07,366
but after eleven at night

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,966
You are lying in bed

6
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:10,233
the lights are already off

7
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:11,666
but the phone is still glowing

8
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:13,233
Your finger swipes down

9
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:15,666
and something suddenly feels like a must have

10
00:00:15,966 --> 00:00:17,666
During the day you had no urge to buy it

11
00:00:17,866 --> 00:00:18,833
but late at night

12
00:00:18,966 --> 00:00:20,366
it seems to whisper to you

13
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,433
just buy it

14
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:23,600
you have had a hard enough day

15
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:26,633
Many think late night shopping is weak willpower

16
00:00:26,866 --> 00:00:27,966
I do not think so

17
00:00:28,266 --> 00:00:30,966
The most counterintuitive part of it is this

18
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:32,766
what you buy is often not the thing itself

19
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:35,300
but compensation for what you swallowed all day

20
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:37,233
During the day you held back too much

21
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:38,900
endured your boss's tone

22
00:00:39,166 --> 00:00:40,600
endured the client's demands

23
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,433
endured the crowded subway

24
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:44,833
endured the frustration you never dared to voice

25
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:45,966
and when night comes

26
00:00:46,066 --> 00:00:48,033
you can finally tap that pay button

27
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:49,400
the tap is light

28
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:51,166
but it feels like telling yourself

29
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,066
at least this one thing is mine to decide

30
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:55,600
This video will not tell you to quit shopping

31
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,833
nor lecture you from above about spending

32
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:00,866
it is about a choice ordinary people face every day

33
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,466
Most impulse buys are not about strong desire

34
00:01:03,566 --> 00:01:05,600
but daytime grievances with no way out

35
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,066
It is midnight

36
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,566
you finally lie down

37
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:11,166
and no one needs you anymore today

38
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:12,800
the work chat has gone quiet

39
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,166
your family is asleep

40
00:01:14,266 --> 00:01:16,233
only you and your phone are left in the room

41
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,900
This moment is dangerous

42
00:01:18,066 --> 00:01:19,666
because you suddenly feel

43
00:01:19,766 --> 00:01:22,066
I finally have a little time to myself

44
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:23,966
During the day you are like a machine

45
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:26,033
reply to messages when you should

46
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:27,666
attend meetings when you should

47
00:01:27,866 --> 00:01:28,966
smile when you should

48
00:01:29,066 --> 00:01:30,066
endure when you should

49
00:01:30,166 --> 00:01:31,266
but late at night

50
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:32,833
you no longer have to play any role

51
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:34,766
you scroll whatever you want

52
00:01:34,766 --> 00:01:36,400
you buy whatever you want

53
00:01:36,466 --> 00:01:39,200
This is what makes late night shopping so gripping

54
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:41,366
it dresses spending up as freedom

55
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:43,300
You are not buying a cup

56
00:01:43,366 --> 00:01:46,233
you are buying the feeling that you can still choose

57
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,233
You are not buying a piece of clothing

58
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:51,433
you are buying a more put together version of tomorrow

59
00:01:51,866 --> 00:01:53,600
You are not buying a snack

60
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:56,966
you are comforting the one who went uncared for all day

61
00:01:57,233 --> 00:01:59,066
If your day went smoothly

62
00:01:59,266 --> 00:02:01,400
you probably scroll a bit and fall asleep

63
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:03,766
but if you were pressed down all day

64
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:05,366
that little bit of buying power at night

65
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:05,933
becomes especially tempting

66
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:06,566
because for most of the day

67
00:02:06,566 --> 00:02:07,100
you were meeting other people's demands

68
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:07,866
only at the moment of ordering

69
00:02:07,866 --> 00:02:08,700
does the world finally move the way you want

70
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,466
This is why so many cannot hold back

71
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:09,866
it is not that the thing is so good

72
00:02:09,866 --> 00:02:10,366
but that the moment of control is so sweet

73
00:02:10,366 --> 00:02:10,833
People most easily pay for a sense of freedom

74
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:11,533
even if it lasts only until the payment goes through

75
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:12,033
There is also a more practical reason

76
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:12,533
your brain is exhausted by daytime

77
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:12,900
choosing what to wear in the morning

78
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:13,300
deciding whose messages to answer on the way

79
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:13,766
figuring out what to do first at work

80
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:14,500
listening to others in meetings

81
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,066
and deciding what to eat after work

82
00:02:15,066 --> 00:02:15,300
all day long

83
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:15,900
your brain keeps making small decisions

84
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:16,633
each one seems minor on its own

85
00:02:16,633 --> 00:02:17,466
but together they slowly drain your patience

86
00:02:17,466 --> 00:02:17,800
and by late night

87
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,233
you no longer want to compare

88
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:18,766
no longer want to weigh if it is worth it

89
00:02:18,766 --> 00:02:19,433
no longer want to ask if you really need it

90
00:02:19,433 --> 00:02:20,033
you just want something to be over quickly

91
00:02:20,033 --> 00:02:20,833
so the platforms love this moment

92
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:21,133
limited time offer

93
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:21,433
ends tonight

94
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:21,666
low in stock

95
00:02:21,666 --> 00:02:22,066
picked for you

96
00:02:22,066 --> 00:02:22,500
others bought it too

97
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:23,166
these words look ordinary by day

98
00:02:23,166 --> 00:02:24,033
but turn powerful late at night

99
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:24,566
because you are tired

100
00:02:24,566 --> 00:02:25,100
tired people dislike complexity

101
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:25,600
tired people like to be pushed along

102
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,066
You may have felt this too

103
00:02:26,066 --> 00:02:26,500
when buying by day

104
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:26,933
you check reviews

105
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:27,166
compare prices

106
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:27,433
ask friends

107
00:02:27,433 --> 00:02:27,900
even leave it in the cart to cool off

108
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:28,300
but buying late at night

109
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:28,666
is often just see it

110
00:02:28,666 --> 00:02:28,866
want it

111
00:02:28,866 --> 00:02:29,233
pay

112
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:29,766
and then you wake up the next day

113
00:02:29,766 --> 00:02:30,233
staring blankly at the order

114
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:30,666
why did I buy this last night

115
00:02:30,666 --> 00:02:31,166
It is not that you suddenly got dumb

116
00:02:31,166 --> 00:02:31,766
it is that the part of you that hits the brakes

117
00:02:31,766 --> 00:02:32,100
is already worn out by night

118
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:32,633
Many sellers are not selling goods

119
00:02:32,633 --> 00:02:33,300
but those few seconds when you are too tired to judge

120
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,100
The moment spending sneaks in

121
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:34,566
is not when you are happiest

122
00:02:34,566 --> 00:02:35,233
but when you are least willing to resist

123
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:35,600
Looking a little deeper

124
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,000
many late night orders

125
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,566
are not really shopping orders

126
00:02:36,566 --> 00:02:37,166
they are emotional orders

127
00:02:37,166 --> 00:02:38,766
Your boss gives you a few harsh words

128
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,833
at night you buy a pricier piece of clothing

129
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:42,633
not because your closet is empty

130
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,900
but because you want to prove you are not that bad

131
00:02:45,233 --> 00:02:47,233
You tend to everyone's feelings all day

132
00:02:47,466 --> 00:02:49,466
at night you order a heavy late snack

133
00:02:49,666 --> 00:02:51,400
not because you are truly starving

134
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:54,200
but because you want to be cared for once

135
00:02:54,366 --> 00:02:56,300
Your life feels stuck lately

136
00:02:56,533 --> 00:02:58,066
so at night you buy a new ornament

137
00:02:58,166 --> 00:02:59,666
not because your home needs it

138
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:02,100
but because you want a little fresh start

139
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:03,900
All of this is understandable

140
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:05,100
people are not account books

141
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:06,300
people need comfort

142
00:03:06,533 --> 00:03:07,466
the problem is

143
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,500
if every comfort comes from paying

144
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:12,833
your emotions get trained into a very costly system

145
00:03:13,033 --> 00:03:13,833
unhappy

146
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:14,533
buy

147
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,333
anxious

148
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:15,966
buy

149
00:03:15,966 --> 00:03:16,633
lonely

150
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:17,233
buy

151
00:03:17,233 --> 00:03:17,866
tired

152
00:03:17,866 --> 00:03:18,500
buy

153
00:03:18,566 --> 00:03:19,533
over time

154
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:21,033
it gets harder to tell apart

155
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,666
whether I really need this thing

156
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:25,100
or I just need someone to hold me

157
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,166
The real danger of late night shopping

158
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:28,666
is not the extra money spent

159
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:30,466
but that it tricks you into believing

160
00:03:30,566 --> 00:03:33,200
every bad mood can be solved by a delivery

161
00:03:33,366 --> 00:03:34,800
but on the day it arrives

162
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,100
you open the box

163
00:03:36,166 --> 00:03:37,366
happy for a few minutes

164
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:39,766
and then life is still the same life

165
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:41,633
the job is still that job

166
00:03:41,866 --> 00:03:43,400
the stress is still that stress

167
00:03:43,566 --> 00:03:44,700
the thing stays

168
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,266
the emotion goes unprocessed

169
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:47,666
and the bill stays too

170
00:03:47,733 --> 00:03:49,766
so you fall into a loop

171
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,200
the more tired the more you buy

172
00:03:51,433 --> 00:03:52,700
the more you buy the more uneasy

173
00:03:52,933 --> 00:03:54,900
the more uneasy the more you want to make up for it

174
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:57,666
in the end you do not own more things

175
00:03:58,033 --> 00:03:59,833
you are reminded by more things

176
00:03:59,966 --> 00:04:01,800
that you failed to take care of yourself again

177
00:04:02,066 --> 00:04:03,666
What truly deserves caution

178
00:04:03,666 --> 00:04:05,633
is not buying something you like once in a while

179
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:09,000
but making spending your only emotional outlet

180
00:04:09,566 --> 00:04:10,833
when the outlet is too narrow

181
00:04:10,933 --> 00:04:12,466
people get dragged along by it

182
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:14,100
There is one more detail

183
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:17,966
Late night buying often follows scrolling short videos

184
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,400
You see someone redo their room

185
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:21,833
someone using a new scent

186
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:24,033
someone heading out in new clothes

187
00:04:24,266 --> 00:04:26,200
someone filming life so light and easy

188
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,766
you watch it lying in bed

189
00:04:27,933 --> 00:04:29,200
thinking it looks nice

190
00:04:29,366 --> 00:04:31,700
while feeling your own life is a bit rough

191
00:04:31,966 --> 00:04:34,566
That gap easily turns into an urge to buy

192
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:37,033
You do not simply want that item

193
00:04:37,433 --> 00:04:40,066
you want to buy away the gap between you and others

194
00:04:40,433 --> 00:04:41,466
but the problem is

195
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,366
others show you the result

196
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:44,900
you are buying a fragment

197
00:04:45,266 --> 00:04:48,000
A cup cannot turn your life into that video

198
00:04:48,333 --> 00:04:51,033
A lamp cannot fix your messy schedule

199
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:54,433
Clothes cannot make you a more relaxed person

200
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:56,466
so many late night orders

201
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:58,300
only lose their magic once they arrive

202
00:04:58,566 --> 00:05:01,000
because what they promised was not function

203
00:05:01,166 --> 00:05:02,833
but an illusion of a life

204
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:04,500
You think you are buying a thing

205
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:07,500
but you buy the fantasy that you could live like that

206
00:05:07,866 --> 00:05:08,966
the fantasy is beautiful

207
00:05:09,066 --> 00:05:11,033
but it rarely ships free to reality

208
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:13,233
What should stop here

209
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,366
is not the cart

210
00:05:14,566 --> 00:05:17,766
but the mind that keeps comparing you to others

211
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,000
If you are already exhausted today

212
00:05:20,233 --> 00:05:22,500
do not let other people's polished lives

213
00:05:22,633 --> 00:05:24,033
keep charging you

214
00:05:24,566 --> 00:05:25,866
So what should ordinary people do

215
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:27,566
not to never buy again

216
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:29,800
nor to live like a monk

217
00:05:30,066 --> 00:05:32,433
but to reclaim the three seconds before paying

218
00:05:32,633 --> 00:05:33,433
First

219
00:05:33,433 --> 00:05:35,700
set a daytime review for late night buys

220
00:05:35,966 --> 00:05:36,966
if you want it at night

221
00:05:37,033 --> 00:05:38,600
put it in the cart first

222
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,066
but do not pay right away

223
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,100
tell yourself

224
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:42,833
if I still want it tomorrow noon

225
00:05:42,833 --> 00:05:43,533
then buy it

226
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:45,166
This method is simple

227
00:05:45,166 --> 00:05:46,166
but it works

228
00:05:46,466 --> 00:05:48,066
because what you truly need

229
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,233
is still there after a night

230
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,266
desires propped up by emotion

231
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,033
often collapse by the next day

232
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:53,900
Second

233
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,233
before paying ask yourself

234
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,766
is it a thing I am short of

235
00:05:56,933 --> 00:05:58,000
or is it rest

236
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:00,266
sometimes what you need is not new clothes

237
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,300
it is an early night

238
00:06:01,466 --> 00:06:02,633
not new headphones

239
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:04,566
but an undisturbed evening

240
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,000
not a late night meal

241
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:07,766
but someone to hear you out

242
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:11,566
This question pulls you from the product page back to yourself

243
00:06:11,833 --> 00:06:12,633
Third

244
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,866
prepare cheap outlets for bad moods

245
00:06:15,033 --> 00:06:16,400
like taking a hot shower

246
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:17,766
walking outside for ten minutes

247
00:06:17,833 --> 00:06:18,800
writing a few lines

248
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,366
tidying a small corner of your room

249
00:06:20,466 --> 00:06:22,666
texting a friend that you are a bit tired today

250
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:23,966
these things are not cool

251
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,000
nor exciting

252
00:06:25,033 --> 00:06:27,366
but they do not turn emotions into bills

253
00:06:27,766 --> 00:06:29,566
Let yourself be comforted

254
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,866
but do not let every comfort charge you

255
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:33,066
Fourth

256
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:35,566
make yourself a free reward list

257
00:06:35,866 --> 00:06:37,566
many people when they say reward myself

258
00:06:37,833 --> 00:06:39,666
immediately picture buying something

259
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,700
but rewards can be cheap

260
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,500
like no overtime tonight

261
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:45,400
like keeping the phone a bit away

262
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:47,400
like watching an episode you love

263
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:50,300
like setting tomorrow's alarm ten minutes later

264
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:52,433
like cooking yourself a bowl of warm soup

265
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:54,566
these rewards are not thrilling

266
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:56,233
but they feel more like care

267
00:06:56,566 --> 00:06:58,766
spending usually gives you excitement

268
00:06:58,966 --> 00:07:00,900
care is what gives you recovery

269
00:07:01,233 --> 00:07:03,000
the better you tell them apart

270
00:07:03,066 --> 00:07:06,100
the less you send every bout of fatigue into the cart

271
00:07:06,566 --> 00:07:08,466
The best decision to make late at night

272
00:07:08,733 --> 00:07:09,733
is not to pay

273
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:10,666
it is to pause

274
00:07:11,166 --> 00:07:13,400
What is truly expensive is not that item

275
00:07:13,666 --> 00:07:16,666
it is your growing habit of numbing pain with money

276
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:19,233
There is an even simpler way

277
00:07:19,566 --> 00:07:22,300
write what you want to buy into one sentence

278
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:23,900
I want to buy this

279
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:26,566
because I want to look better

280
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,166
I want to buy this

281
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,166
because I am too tired today

282
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,766
I want to buy this

283
00:07:31,866 --> 00:07:34,433
because I do not want to admit I am a little lonely

284
00:07:34,866 --> 00:07:35,966
Once you write it down

285
00:07:36,033 --> 00:07:38,800
many orders reveal their real names

286
00:07:39,133 --> 00:07:40,366
it is not called a cup

287
00:07:40,466 --> 00:07:42,033
it is called wanting a fresh start

288
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,466
it is not called clothes

289
00:07:43,533 --> 00:07:44,833
it is called wanting to be seen

290
00:07:45,133 --> 00:07:46,300
it is not called a snack

291
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,366
it is called no one comforted me today

292
00:07:48,666 --> 00:07:50,466
When you can say its real name

293
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:53,300
you no longer have to solve it by paying

294
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:55,666
some desires once seen

295
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:57,066
grow a little quieter

296
00:07:57,366 --> 00:07:59,400
some grievances once acknowledged

297
00:07:59,566 --> 00:08:01,466
no longer rush to become a delivery

298
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:04,166
So what late night shopping really trains

299
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:05,200
is not holding back

300
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:06,566
but understanding yourself

301
00:08:06,966 --> 00:08:08,000
once you understand

302
00:08:08,133 --> 00:08:09,800
you can decide tomorrow

303
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:12,433
you can care for yourself another way

304
00:08:12,766 --> 00:08:14,700
you can even do nothing

305
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:16,066
just go to bed early

306
00:08:16,366 --> 00:08:17,233
many times

307
00:08:17,533 --> 00:08:19,033
the you who wakes up tomorrow

308
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:22,066
will thank the you who did not pay last night

309
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:25,600
that is a cheaper and cleaner kind of freedom

310
00:08:25,766 --> 00:08:28,033
and more like real self care

311
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,700
Late night buying is not a sin

312
00:08:29,966 --> 00:08:31,300
it is just a reminder

313
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:33,466
reminding you your day was too tight

314
00:08:33,666 --> 00:08:36,166
reminding you it has been too long since you cared for yourself

315
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,600
reminding you that you may not need more goods

316
00:08:39,766 --> 00:08:42,366
but more room to breathe

317
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:44,500
What one should reclaim most

318
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:46,466
is not the discipline of never spending

319
00:08:46,666 --> 00:08:49,566
but the clarity to see what you truly need

320
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,500
Next time we will talk about takeout

321
00:08:51,666 --> 00:08:53,433
why takeout keeps getting more expensive

322
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,833
it is not always that sellers turned bad

323
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:57,100
many times

324
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,600
what you buy is not a meal

325
00:08:58,733 --> 00:09:01,000
but the trouble someone saved you from

326
00:09:01,233 --> 00:09:02,300
See you next time
